{title: Remain in Me}
{subtitle: John 15:1–8}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Father is the gardener who tends [Eb]the vine with [Bb]care
He takes away the barren wood and prunes [F]the branches there
So [Gm7]every branch that bears [Eb]its fruit will bear [Bb]its [Bbmaj7/A]fruit the [Gm7]more
[Eb]And we are clean [Bb]already by the word [F]he spoke be[Bb]fore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am the [Eb]vine; you are the branch[Bb]es
Whoever remains [Eb]in me and I [F]in him bears [Bb]much fruit
[F]For [Eb]apart from [F]me you can [Gm]do noth[Eb]ing
Remain in [F]me, and I in [Bb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Gm7] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A branch can't bear fruit by itself, it needs [Eb]the vine to [Bb]grow
It withers when it's broken off and lies [F]in dust below
But [Gm]if you stay with me, [Eb]he said, and my [Bb]words in [F/A]you re[Gm7]main
Then [Eb]ask whatever [Bb]you may wish, you will [F]not ask in [Bb]vain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I [Bb/D]am the [Eb]vine; you are the branch[Bb]es
Whoever re[Eb]mains in me and [F]I in him [Bb]bears much [F]fruit
For [Eb]apart from [F]me you can [Gm]do noth[Eb]ing
Remain in [F]me, and I in [Bb]you [Bbmaj7/A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]This is how my [Eb]Father is [Bb]glori[F]fied
[Gm]That you bear [Eb]much fruit
[Bb]And so prove to be [F]my disciples
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Re[Eb]main in [F]me, and I in [Bb]you
I [Bb/D]am the [Eb]vine; you are the branch[Bb]es
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
